wxChaos Changelog
------------------
- Version 2.0.0
	- Major codebase rewrite.
	- Complete UI redesign.
	- Dark theme.
	- Standardized rendering algorithms. Now most fractals can use the same rendering algorithms.
	- Created documentation for each fractal.
	- Added viewport manipulation tools.
	- Smooth zooming.
	- Added settings menu.
	- Added Newton Raphson user formula.
	- Improved zoom recorder precision.
	- Command console improvements: Better syntax, autocompletion, history.
	- Improved threading performance.
	- Miscellaneous crash bugfixes.
	- New color palettes and color mapping.
	- Implemented multiprecision. That means that users can perform infinite zooms.
	- Implemented perturbation rendering in Mandelbrot and Julia sets. That means that infinite zooms are faster.

- Version 1.1.0
	- Linux: Modified the installing directories according to the Ubuntu store guidelines.

- Version 1.0.3
	- Switched to the double precision model on the scripting language.
	- Script fractals now plot on "x" and "y" instead of "real" and "imaginary".
	- Added cut billiard fractal.
	- Fixed a linking problem on Ubuntu 13.04

- Version 1.0.2
	- Fixed a bug on the WASD navigation.

- Version 1.0.1
	- Added support for unicode build.
	- Parser now reports errors.
	- Fixed bug that made Julia Mode crash.
	- "AddLine" command added.
	- Fixed Show Orbit bug that made some lines to be rendered incorrectly.
	- Various bugfixes.
	- Linux support.
